## Pattern 6: If you pay before you have the thing, you probably won't get the thing

{Open-paragraph on the country's OTA / ticket-reseller / WhatsApp-payment risk surface}

{2-3 paragraphs of specific pre-payment scams: booking fraud, fake-tour fraud, deposit-then-vanish fraud, currency-switch fraud}

The defense is a set of habits that apply to every transaction you make in {COUNTRY}:

- **Book accommodation** only through platforms with chargeback guarantees (Booking.com, Agoda, Airbnb, Expedia) — never via {country-specific-chat-app} or personal bank transfer
- **Book tickets** only through named-Ministry-licensed operators or top-tier OTAs
- **Pay by credit card** (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), never by debit card, cash, or direct transfer
